<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_PA-03.3-vendor-performance-and-contracts" targetNamespace="https://erpplans.local/bpmn" exporter="erpplans generate-bpmn.py" exporterVersion="1.0">
    <bpmn:process id="W_W959" name="W959. Vendor Rebate Volume Tier Compliance Reconciliation &amp; Shortfall Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly/quarterly vendor rebate period closes; system reconciles actual purchase volume against rebate agreement tier thresholds
Frequency: ~200–300 reconciliations/quarter (for vendors with tiered rebate agreements)
Volume: 1 vendor per reconciliation; multi-tier agreements (e.g., 3% at PHP 1M, 5% at PHP 3M, 7% at PHP 5M quarterly)
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Buyer, Finance Analyst, Vendor Account Manager, VP Merchandising, AP Manager
Source: workflow W959 — Vendor Rebate Volume Tier Compliance Reconciliation &amp; Shortfall Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W959_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W959_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W959_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W959_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W959_Lane2" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W959_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W959_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W959_Lane3" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W959_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W959_Lane4" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W959_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W959_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W959_Start6" name="Monthly/quarterly vendor rebate period closes; system reconciles actual purchase volume…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W959_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W959_Task7" name="Period-End Volume Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Period-End Volume Calculation: At rebate period close (monthly or quarterly per agreement): (a) system extracts all purchase volume (PO value at cost) per vendor from AP module per W7; (b) matches against vendor rebate agreement terms: (i) agreement period start/end; (ii) tier thresholds (e.g., PHP 1M/3M/5M); (iii) rebate rate per tier (e.g., 3%/5%/7%); (iv) eligible product categories (some agreements exclude clearance or consignment); (v) exclusion rules (returns, credits, sample items); (c) system calculates: actual qualifying volume, applicable tier, earned rebate amount, and variance to next tier (up or down)
Responsible (R): System / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/vendor (automated calculation + manual review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W959_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W959_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W959_Task8" name="Tier Achievement Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Tier Achievement Assessment: Finance Analyst reviews each vendor&#x27;s tier status: (a) tier maintained (e.g., qualified for 5% tier, same as last period) → routine processing; (b) tier upgraded (e.g., qualified for 7% tier, up from 5%) → calculate incremental rebate income; (c) tier downgraded (e.g., qualified for 3% tier, down from 5%) → calculate lost rebate income and investigate volume decline; (d) near-miss analysis: vendor fell short of next tier by ≤ 10% — flag for Buyer review: could accelerated purchasing have pushed volume into next tier?; (e) system generates tier achievement report per vendor with variance analysis
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W959_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W959_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W959_Task9" name="Shortfall Investigation &amp; Vendor Negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Shortfall Investigation &amp; Vendor Negotiation: For tier downgrades and significant near-misses: (a) Buyer investigates volume decline: (i) SKU discontinuations per W68 reducing purchases; (ii) competitive vendor gains (purchases shifted to alternative vendor); (iii) store-level stock balancing reducing replenishment orders; (iv) seasonal demand decline; (b) for tier downgrades: Buyer contacts vendor to negotiate: (i) retroactive tier maintenance with purchase commitment for next period; (ii) extended transition period (vendor grants old tier for one more period); (iii) revised tier thresholds reflecting current market conditions; (c) negotiation outcome documented in vendor rebate agreement with updated terms per W62; (d) for near-misses: Buyer reviews upcoming purchase requirements — if sufficient volume expected early next period, may negotiate &quot;rollover&quot; credit
Responsible (R): Buyer / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours/vendor (for downgrade/near-miss)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W959_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W959_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W959_Task10" name="Rebate Accrual Adjustment &amp; Financial Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Rebate Accrual Adjustment &amp; Financial Processing: (a) Finance adjusts rebate accrual per W27: (i) for tier upgrade — increase accrual rate to new tier for current and forward periods; (ii) for tier downgrade — decrease accrual rate; true-up prior period accrual at old rate to actual earned rebate; (iii) true-up amount posted to P&amp;L as rebate income adjustment; (b) AP Manager processes vendor rebate settlement per W767: system generates rebate claim with calculated amount based on actual tier achievement; vendor verifies and pays rebate per agreed timeline (30–60 days); (c) Finance reconciles: rebate claimed vs. rebate received vs. rebate accrued; variance investigated per W100 vendor statement reconciliation
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / AP Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 15–30 min/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W959_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W959_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W959_Task11" name="Quarterly Rebate Portfolio Optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Rebate Portfolio Optimization: (a) Category Manager reviews rebate portfolio: (i) total rebate income vs. target; (ii) tier achievement rate across all vendors (target: ≥ 80% at committed tier or above); (iii) top 10 vendors by rebate income; (iv) vendors with declining purchase volumes trending toward downgrade; (v) vendors where BuildRight is purchasing below tier potential; (b) VP Merchandising reviews: (i) opportunities to consolidate purchases with fewer vendors to achieve higher tiers (volume concentration vs. vendor diversification trade-off per W763); (ii) renegotiation schedule for agreements approaching expiry; (iii) proactive purchase acceleration at period-end for near-miss vendors (weighing carrying cost per W220 vs. incremental rebate income); (c) annual: Finance includes vendor rebate income in category P&amp;L analysis per W102
Responsible (R): Category Manager / VP Merchandising / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising / CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W959_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W959_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W959_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W959_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W959_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W959_Assoc14" sourceRef="W959_Annotation13" targetRef="W959_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
