    <bpmn:process id="W_W962" name="W962. Vendor-Sponsored In-Store Display Compliance Audit &amp; Chargeback" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly display compliance audit cycle; or vendor reports display not meeting contractual requirements
Frequency: ~400–600 display audits/month (covering ~200 vendor-sponsored displays across 200 stores)
Volume: 1–5 displays audited per store per month
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Department Supervisor (store), Category Manager, Visual Merchandising Coordinator, Vendor Account Manager, Finance (chargeback processing)
Source: workflow W962 — Vendor-Sponsored In-Store Display Compliance Audit &amp; Chargeback</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W962_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W962_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W962_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W962_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W962_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W962_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W962_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W962_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W962_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W962_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W962_Start4" name="Monthly display compliance audit cycle; or vendor reports display not meeting contractual…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W962_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W962_Task5" name="Monthly Display Audit Schedule">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly Display Audit Schedule: Category Manager generates monthly audit schedule: (a) all active vendor-sponsored displays across 200 stores listed by vendor, store, and display type; (b) audit priority: (i) new displays (installed within last 60 days — highest priority); (ii) displays with previous non-compliance findings; (iii) high-value display agreements (≥ PHP 20,000/month); (iv) random sample of remaining displays (30%); (c) audit assignments distributed to Department Supervisors via mobile task management; (d) target: all high-priority displays audited within first 2 weeks of month; random sample completed by month-end
Responsible (R): Category Manager / System
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W962_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W962_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W962_Task6" name="In-Store Display Audit Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: In-Store Display Audit Execution: Department Supervisor conducts physical audit per display: (a) photographs display from 3 angles (front, side, product close-up) using mobile audit app; (b) checks compliance criteria per vendor agreement: (i) location — display in contracted zone per store layout plan; (ii) product assortment — correct SKUs, minimum facing quantities, no competitor products in display area; (iii) signage — current promotional signage, no expired materials, vendor branding intact; (iv) stock level — display adequately stocked (no empty facings); (v) condition — clean, organized, no damaged products or fixtures; (vi) pricing — correct prices displayed per W69 price compliance; (c) records findings in audit app: compliant (pass), minor non-compliance (advisory), major non-compliance (requires corrective action), critical non-compliance (display fee at risk)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/display</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W962_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W962_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W962_Task7" name="Non-Compliance Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Non-Compliance Resolution: For non-compliant displays: (a) system routes findings to: (i) Visual Merchandising Coordinator — for display setup/condition issues; (ii) Store Manager — for stock replenishment issues; (iii) Category Manager — for product assortment issues; (iv) Vendor — for vendor-provided material/signage issues; (b) corrective action timeline: (i) critical — 48 hours; (ii) major — 7 days; (iii) minor — 14 days (advisory only, no fee impact); (c) Department Supervisor re-audits after corrective action deadline; (d) if non-compliance persists after corrective action deadline: escalates to Category Manager for chargeback processing
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Visual Merchandising Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/non-compliance</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W962_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W962_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W962_Task8" name="Chargeback Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Chargeback Processing: For persistent non-compliance: (a) Category Manager authorizes chargeback per vendor agreement: (i) partial display fee reduction (e.g., 25% for minor compliance gaps); (ii) full display fee forfeiture for critical non-compliance (e.g., display removed, wrong location, competitor products); (iii) damage assessment for vendor-provided fixtures damaged by BuildRight staff; (b) Finance processes chargeback per W245 vendor chargebacks: (i) debit memo issued to vendor; (ii) display fee reduced by chargeback amount; (iii) vendor notified via W705 vendor portal with audit evidence (photos, compliance checklist); (c) vendor dispute resolution per W869 vendor dispute ticketing — vendor can contest chargeback with evidence; (d) Category Manager adjudicates disputes; VP Merchandising escalates unresolved disputes
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30–60 min/chargeback</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W962_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W962_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W962_Task9" name="Quarterly Vendor Display Performance Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Vendor Display Performance Review: (a) Category Manager reviews display compliance portfolio: (i) compliance rate by vendor (target: ≥ 90% compliant); (ii) repeat offenders — vendors with &lt; 80% compliance for 2+ consecutive months; (iii) BuildRight-side non-compliance — stores failing to maintain agreed display conditions (impacts vendor relationship and renewal); (b) VP Merchandising shares compliance data with vendor at quarterly business review per W155 Joint Business Planning; (c) annual: display agreement renewals incorporate compliance history — vendors with strong compliance may negotiate better display locations; vendors with poor compliance face higher scrutiny or non-renewal
Responsible (R): Category Manager / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W962_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W962_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W962_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W962_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W962_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W962_Assoc12" sourceRef="W962_Annotation11" targetRef="W962_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
