    <bpmn:process id="W_W1033" name="W1033. Vendor Lead Time Accuracy Monitoring &amp; Supply Planning Impact Assessment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly scheduled analysis; also triggered by significant lead time deviation detected during PO monitoring
Frequency: Weekly analysis; monthly vendor review; quarterly trend reporting
Volume: ~800–1,000 active vendors with purchase orders; ~1,200 merchandise POs/month
Owner: Supply Chain Planner
Participants: Buyer, Category Manager, DC Receiving Supervisor, Procurement Specialist
Source: workflow W1033 — Vendor Lead Time Accuracy Monitoring &amp; Supply Planning Impact Assessment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1033_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1033_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1033_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1033_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1033_Lane2" name="Supply Chain Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1033_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1033_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1033_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1033_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1033_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1033_Start4" name="Weekly scheduled analysis; also triggered by significant lead time deviation detected…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1033_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1033_Task5" name="Weekly Lead Time Deviation Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly Lead Time Deviation Calculation: System automatically calculates for each PO closed in the past week: (a) Stated lead time (from vendor master per W287): days between PO date and expected delivery date; (b) Actual lead time: days between PO date and goods receipt date at DC/store per W3/W109; (c) Deviation = (Actual − Stated) ÷ Stated × 100; (d) system aggregates by vendor: average deviation, standard deviation, on-time delivery rate (% of POs received within stated lead time + 3 day tolerance); (e) weekly vendor lead time scorecard generated: Tier 1 (Accurate): deviation ≤ 10%, on-time ≥ 90%; Tier 2 (Variable): deviation 10–25%, on-time 70–90%; Tier 3 (Unreliable): deviation &gt; 25%, on-time &lt; 70%
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Supply Chain Planner
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1033_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1033_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1033_Task6" name="Planning Parameter Adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Planning Parameter Adjustment: For vendors consistently deviating from stated lead time: (a) if vendor has been Tier 2 (Variable) for 2+ consecutive weeks: Supply Chain Planner adjusts the vendor&#x27;s lead time parameter in the replenishment system (W312) to reflect actual average lead time + safety buffer; this immediately adjusts reorder points for all SKUs sourced from this vendor; (b) if vendor has been Tier 3 (Unreliable) for 2+ consecutive weeks: (i) increase safety stock for all affected SKUs by 1–2 weeks of demand to buffer against uncertainty; (ii) evaluate alternative sourcing per W921 (Emergency Alternative Vendor) for critical SKUs; (iii) Buyer escalates to vendor per W44 (Vendor Performance Review); (c) parameter changes logged in system with justification; system generates impact analysis: estimated inventory value change from parameter adjustment (increase in safety stock = additional carrying cost)
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30–60 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1033_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1033_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1033_Task7" name="Stockout Root Cause Analysis (Lead Time Related)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Stockout Root Cause Analysis (Lead Time Related): When a stockout occurs: (a) system checks if the stockout was caused by a late vendor delivery (PO past due with no GR); (b) if yes: flag the stockout as &quot;lead time related&quot; and attribute to the specific vendor and PO; (c) calculate lost sales impact: stockout duration × average daily sales velocity × average margin; (d) weekly stockout report includes lead-time-related stockout attribution by vendor; (e) vendors responsible for &gt; 5% of total chain-wide stockouts in a month are flagged for Buyer review per W44
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1033_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1033_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1033_Task8" name="Monthly Vendor Lead Time Review Meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly Vendor Lead Time Review Meeting: Monthly meeting between Supply Chain Planner, Buyer, and Category Manager: (a) review top 20 vendors by lead time deviation (worst performers); (b) for each: discuss root cause — production delay, shipping issue, customs hold, order processing error, or seasonal pattern; (c) agree on action: (i) renegotiate lead time commitment with vendor (adjust vendor master to realistic lead time), (ii) vendor improvement plan with milestones per W110 (CAPA), (iii) dual-source strategy per W763 (Vendor Diversification), (iv) vendor exit and replacement per W36/W62; (d) review top 20 vendors by volume (regardless of deviation) to ensure lead time parameters are current for high-value POs; (e) decisions documented and tracked in vendor performance module
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner / Buyer / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 60–90 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1033_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1033_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1033_Task9" name="Quarterly Trend Analysis &amp; Network Impact Report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Trend Analysis &amp; Network Impact Report: Supply Chain Planner compiles quarterly report: (a) chain-wide lead time accuracy trend: average deviation, % of vendors in each tier, improvement/degradation vs. prior quarter; (b) financial impact: estimated carrying cost from inflated safety stock (step 2) vs. lost sales from lead-time-related stockouts (step 3); (c) seasonal patterns: import vendors during Chinese New Year (Feb), typhoon season (Jul–Nov), Christmas peak (Oct–Dec) — lead time degradation patterns; (d) strategic recommendations: nearshoring opportunities (replace China imports with Philippines/ASEAN vendors for shorter lead times), vendor consolidation, or inventory strategy changes (VMI expansion per W20); (e) report presented to VP Supply Chain and COO for strategic planning per W127
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1033_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1033_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1033_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1033_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1033_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: should track import PO lead times separately from local POs with wider tolerance bands
Owner: Supply Chain Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1033_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1033_Annotation11" targetRef="W1033_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
