    <bpmn:process id="W_W1115" name="W1115. Vendor Performance-Based Shelf Space Allocation Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Semi-annual planogram review cycle, vendor scorecard quarterly publication (W871), or category performance review (W101)
Frequency: Semi-annual (major review); quarterly (minor adjustments)
Volume: ~800–1,000 active vendors × ~2.5–3 product categories each (of the 12-category universe) = ~2,000–3,000 vendor-category combinations reviewed per cycle
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Planogram Analyst, Merchandise Planner, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1115 — Vendor Performance-Based Shelf Space Allocation Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1115_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1115_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1115_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1115_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1115_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1115_Lane2" name="Planogram Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1115_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1115_Lane3" name="Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1115_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1115_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1115_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1115_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1115_Start6" name="Semi-annual planogram review cycle, vendor scorecard quarterly publication (W871), or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1115_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1115_Task7" name="Vendor Performance Scorecard Compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor Performance Scorecard Compilation: (a) Category Manager compiles composite vendor performance score for each vendor in their category: Sales Performance (40% weight): sales velocity (units/week/facing), sales growth YoY, revenue per sqm of allocated shelf space, contribution to category gross margin; Supply Reliability (25% weight): fill rate % (orders fulfilled complete and on-time), lead time accuracy, VMI program compliance (if applicable), ASN accuracy; Marketing Support (20% weight): co-op advertising spend, demo/event participation, new product introduction pipeline, trade fund utilization (W738); Strategic Fit (15% weight): brand strength and consumer demand, sustainability/ESG compliance, innovation (new product development), exclusivity agreements; (b) scores normalized on a 100-point scale per vendor per category; (c) vendors ranked within each category; (d) top 20% = &quot;Premier&quot; vendors, middle 50% = &quot;Core&quot; vendors, bottom 30% = &quot;Review&quot; vendors
Responsible (R): Category Manager / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/category × 12 categories = 48–72 hours total</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1115_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1115_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1115_Task8" name="Shelf Space Allocation Modeling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Shelf Space Allocation Modeling: (a) Planogram Analyst uses planogram software to model space allocation scenarios: (i) Current state: existing facings and positions for each vendor; (ii) Performance-based model: shelf space proportional to composite score — Premier vendors get 150% of current space, Core vendors maintain 100%, Review vendors reduced to 50–75%; (iii) Revenue-optimized model: space allocated purely by sales per sqm, ignoring vendor relationship factors; (b) for each model, system calculates: projected category revenue, projected category gross margin, number of SKUs changes (additions/removals), number of planogram resets required per store; (c) Category Manager selects preferred model or hybrid: typically performance-based with strategic exceptions (e.g., a new vendor given minimum display space for trial period, or a high-margin vendor protected despite lower velocity)
Responsible (R): Planogram Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 8–12 hours/category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1115_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1115_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1115_Task9" name="Vendor Communication &amp; Negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor Communication &amp; Negotiation: (a) for &quot;Premier&quot; vendors: Category Manager meets to confirm expanded shelf space and discuss additional support opportunities (larger endcaps, demo events, co-branded promotions); (b) for &quot;Core&quot; vendors: standard communication via vendor portal (W871) with scorecard results and any minor space adjustments; (c) for &quot;Review&quot; vendors: formal meeting to discuss: (i) specific performance gaps and improvement timeline (90 days); (ii) potential shelf space reduction if performance does not improve; (iii) delisting timeline if vendor falls below minimum threshold for two consecutive reviews; (iv) remediation plan: vendor may propose additional marketing support, improved fill rate, or new exclusive products to justify maintaining current space; (d) all agreements documented in vendor business plan addendum
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising (for delisting decisions)
Duration: 1–2 hours per Review vendor; 30 min per Premier vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1115_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1115_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1115_Task10" name="Planogram Reset Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Planogram Reset Execution: (a) updated planograms distributed to all 200 stores per W573 (planogram execution &amp; shelf compliance check); (b) shelf labels and product positions updated during overnight reset or during designated reset window; (c) Store Compliance: Store Manager confirms planogram compliance within 7 days; (d) Regional Manager audits 10% of stores for compliance within 14 days per W86; (e) system tracks compliance rate: target ≥ 95% of stores compliant within 7 days
Responsible (R): Store Operations / Planogram Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 days per store per reset</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1115_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1115_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1115_Task11" name="Post-Reset Performance Tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-Reset Performance Tracking: (a) system monitors category performance for 8 weeks post-reset: (i) sales per sqm vs. pre-reset baseline; (ii) gross margin per sqm; (iii) customer traffic in affected sections; (iv) vendor fill rate changes (did Review vendors improve?); (b) results shared with VP Merchandising for quarterly review; (c) lessons learned inform next semi-annual allocation cycle
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours/cycle for analysis</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1115_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1115_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1115_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1115_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1115_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1115_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1115_Annotation13" targetRef="W1115_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1115_Flow15" sourceRef="W1115_Start6" targetRef="W1115_Task7" />
