    <bpmn:process id="W_W1132" name="W1132. Vendor Logistics Performance Weekly Scorecard &amp; Carrier Lane Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly logistics performance review cycle (every Monday), or carrier SLA breach alert
Frequency: Weekly review; continuous monitoring
Volume: ~800–1,000 active vendor-carrier lanes reviewed weekly
Owner: Logistics Manager (HQ)
Participants: Logistics Manager, Supply Chain Planners, DC Operations Managers, Vendor Logistics Contacts
Source: workflow W1132 — Vendor Logistics Performance Weekly Scorecard &amp; Carrier Lane Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1132_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1132_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1132_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1132_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1132_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1132_Lane2" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1132_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1132_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1132_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1132_Start4" name="Weekly logistics performance review cycle (every Monday), or carrier SLA breach alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1132_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1132_Task5" name="Weekly Data Aggregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly Data Aggregation: (a) system auto-aggregates logistics performance data for the previous week: on-time delivery rate (OTD) per vendor per lane; transit time actual vs. promised; delivery appointment compliance (delivered within scheduled window); damage/shortage rate per carrier; freight cost per unit/km by lane; demurrage/detention charges incurred; container turnaround time (for imports); (b) data sourced from: ERP PO and GR modules, fleet telematics (W199), DC dock scheduling system (W585), carrier invoice data, customs brokerage records
Responsible (R): System / Logistics Analyst
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Automated (30 min review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1132_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1132_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1132_Task6" name="Scorecard Generation &amp; Lane Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Scorecard Generation &amp; Lane Analysis: (a) system generates weekly scorecard: top 20 vendors by PO volume — OTD, lead time accuracy, damage rate; top 10 carrier lanes by volume — cost, transit time, reliability; exception report — any lane with OTD &lt; 90%, damage &gt; 2%, or cost &gt; 10% above benchmark; new carrier options — market rate comparison for underperforming lanes; seasonal lane performance — compare current vs. same period last year; (b) lane heat map: green (OTD &gt; 95%, damage &lt; 1%), yellow (OTD 85–95%, damage 1–2%), red (OTD &lt; 85%, damage &gt; 2%)
Responsible (R): System / Logistics Analyst
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 30–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1132_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1132_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1132_Task7" name="Performance Review &amp; Action Items">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Performance Review &amp; Action Items: (a) Logistics Manager reviews scorecard with Supply Chain Planners and DC Operations Managers; (b) red lanes: root cause analysis — carrier capacity issue, vendor readiness problem, DC scheduling conflict, or infrastructure constraint (port congestion, road conditions); (c) action items: carrier escalation meeting (within 5 business days), vendor compliance notice per W669, DC scheduling adjustment, alternative carrier activation, or route optimization per W196; (d) yellow lanes: monitor for trend — if declining for 3+ consecutive weeks, escalate to red; (e) green lanes: identify best practices for replication; (f) cost optimization: identify lanes where competitive quoting could save &gt; 5% without service degradation
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / Supply Chain Planners
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 60–90 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1132_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1132_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1132_Task8" name="Vendor &amp; Carrier Communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Vendor &amp; Carrier Communication: (a) weekly performance summary shared with top 20 vendors via vendor portal (W871); (b) SLA breach notifications sent automatically to vendor and carrier contacts; (c) quarterly business review (QBR) invitations sent to strategic vendor-carrier partners; (d) carrier rate negotiation initiated for lanes with consistent overcharges
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / Vendor Manager
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1132_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1132_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1132_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1132_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1132_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: Logistics Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Logistics Manager (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1132_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1132_Annotation10" targetRef="W1132_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1132_Flow12" sourceRef="W1132_Start4" targetRef="W1132_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1132_Flow13" sourceRef="W1132_Task5" targetRef="W1132_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1132_Flow14" sourceRef="W1132_Task6" targetRef="W1132_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1132_Flow15" sourceRef="W1132_Task7" targetRef="W1132_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1132_Flow16" sourceRef="W1132_Task8" targetRef="W1132_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1132_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1132_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1132">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1132_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1132_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1132_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1132_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1132_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1132_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1132_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1132_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1132_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1141" name="W1141. Vendor Payment Term Annual Renegotiation &amp; Cost Savings Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual vendor contract renewal cycle, or quarterly vendor business review, or significant volume growth with a vendor
Frequency: ~200–300 renegotiations/year (top vendors reviewed annually; others reviewed every 2–3 years)
Volume: 1 vendor per negotiation
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Buyer, Finance Manager, VP Merchandising, Vendor Account Manager
Source: workflow W1141 — Vendor Payment Term Annual Renegotiation &amp; Cost Savings Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1141_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1141_Lane1" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1141_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1141_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1141_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1141_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1141_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1141_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1141_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1141_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1141_Start4" name="Annual vendor contract renewal cycle, or quarterly vendor business review, or significant…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1141_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1141_Task5" name="Vendor Portfolio Analysis &amp; Prioritization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor Portfolio Analysis &amp; Prioritization: (a) Finance Manager and Category Manager jointly review vendor portfolio: total annual spend per vendor, current payment terms (Net 30, Net 60, 2/10 Net 30, LC, etc.), payment term benchmark vs. industry standard, vendor concentration risk, vendor strategic importance (exclusive products, VMI, innovation partner); (b) prioritize vendors for renegotiation: Tier 1 (top 20 vendors by spend) — mandatory annual review; Tier 2 (top 21–100) — review every 2 years; Tier 3 (remaining) — review as needed or at contract renewal; (c) set negotiation targets per vendor: payment term extension (e.g., Net 30 → Net 60), early payment discount (e.g., 2/10 Net 30 → 3/10 Net 30), or combination
Responsible (R): Finance Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hours (annual)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1141_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1141_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1141_Task6" name="Negotiation Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Negotiation Preparation: (a) Category Manager prepares negotiation package for each target vendor: current terms, proposed terms, business rationale (volume growth, expanded assortment, multi-year commitment), competitive benchmarking (what terms do comparable retailers receive), BuildRight&#x27;s value proposition (200-store network, growing ecommerce channel, marketing partnership opportunities); (b) Finance Manager models financial impact: working capital benefit of term extension, COGS savings from discount improvement, impact on vendor relationship if terms are pushed too hard; (c) identify trade-offs: if vendor won&#x27;t extend terms, what else can be negotiated (rebate increase, marketing fund contribution, exclusive product access, VMI expansion)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1141_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1141_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1141_Task7" name="Vendor Negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor Negotiation: (a) Category Manager leads negotiation with vendor account manager; (b) present data-driven proposal: &quot;Our volume has grown 15% YoY, and we&#x27;re expanding to 300 stores. We&#x27;d like to move from Net 30 to Net 60, which is standard for our volume tier. In return, we&#x27;re offering a 3-year commitment on your core assortment and priority placement in our ecommerce platform&quot;; (c) negotiation tactics: volume-based leverage, multi-year commitment incentive, competitive vendor comparison (without naming competitors), early payment discount as alternative to term extension; (d) Finance Manager joins for complex negotiations (LC terms, import payment restructuring); (e) target outcome: improved terms with mutual benefit (vendor gets volume commitment, BuildRight gets better cash management)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1141_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1141_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1141_Task8" name="Agreement Finalization &amp; ERP Update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Agreement Finalization &amp; ERP Update: (a) negotiated terms documented in updated vendor agreement per W62; (b) legal review per W230 for significant changes; (c) ERP vendor master updated with new payment terms (W287, W295); (d) system validates new terms against existing open POs and invoices; (e) implementation timeline: immediate for new POs, transitional for existing open orders; (f) new terms communicated to AP team for payment run configuration (W556)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance Manager / AP Team
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30–60 min per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1141_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1141_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1141_Task9" name="Cost Savings Tracking &amp; Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cost Savings Tracking &amp; Reporting: (a) Finance Manager tracks realized savings from renegotiated terms: working capital improvement (days payable outstanding change × daily COGS), early payment discount capture rate improvement, rebate/pricing improvements achieved as part of negotiation; (b) monthly report to VP Merchandising and CFO: total annualized savings from payment term negotiations, savings by vendor and category, working capital impact; (c) savings feed into category P&amp;L reporting (W102) and procurement KPIs (W633 PPV); (d) lessons learned documented for future negotiation cycles
Responsible (R): Finance Manager / System
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1141_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1141_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1141_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1141_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1141_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: controls needed to prevent early or late payments that violate agreements
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1141_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1141_Annotation11" targetRef="W1141_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
