    <bpmn:process id="W_W1151" name="W1151. Vendor Product Recall Cost Recovery &amp; Margin Impact Assessment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Product recall event (W29, W873–W878), or quarterly recall cost reconciliation, or vendor negotiation session
Frequency: ~5–15 recall events/year requiring cost recovery; quarterly reconciliation
Volume: 1–50 affected SKUs per recall event
Owner: Category Manager (HQ)
Participants: Category Manager, Finance Analyst, Supply Chain Planner, Vendor Representative, Legal Counsel (if disputed)
Source: workflow W1151 — Vendor Product Recall Cost Recovery &amp; Margin Impact Assessment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1151_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1151_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1151_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1151_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1151_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1151_Lane2" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1151_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1151_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1151_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1151_Start4" name="Product recall event (W29, W873–W878), or quarterly recall cost reconciliation, or vendor…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1151_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1151_Task5" name="Recall Cost Capture &amp; Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Recall Cost Capture &amp; Documentation: (a) when a recall is initiated (W873), Category Manager opens a recall cost tracker in ERP; (b) system begins automatic cost capture for the recall event: inventory value of quarantined stock (at WAC), return processing labor hours × hourly rate, reverse logistics costs (pickup from stores, DC handling, vendor return shipping), regulatory filing costs (DTI notifications, BIR adjustments), replacement procurement cost differential (if alternative vendor price is higher); (c) Category Manager captures indirect costs: store labor hours spent on recall activities, estimated lost sales during shelf gap, customer complaint handling costs (W41), temporary price reduction on substitute items
Responsible (R): Category Manager / System
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing during recall</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1151_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1151_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1151_Task6" name="Margin Impact Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Margin Impact Assessment: (a) finance analyst calculates margin impact: gross margin on recalled items (before recall) vs. gross margin on replacement items (after recall); (b) if replacement sourced from alternative vendor at higher cost but sold at same retail price: margin erosion quantified per unit and projected over expected remaining sales period; (c) if replacement sourced from same vendor at same cost but recall caused shelf gap period: lost sales margin calculated (days off-shelf × average daily units × margin %); (d) total margin impact = direct recall costs + indirect costs + margin erosion on replacements + lost sales during gap; (e) margin impact report generated for executive review and vendor claim preparation
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours per recall</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1151_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1151_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1151_Task7" name="Vendor Cost Recovery Claim">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor Cost Recovery Claim: (a) Category Manager prepares vendor cost recovery claim using recall cost tracker data; (b) claim includes: itemized direct costs with supporting documentation (GRNs, shipping invoices, labor logs), margin erosion calculation with market data (alternative vendor quotes), regulatory compliance costs with receipts, total claim amount; (c) claim submitted to vendor per terms of vendor agreement (W62 — contract terms, W244 — dispute resolution); (d) standard recovery expectation: 80–100% of direct costs, 50–75% of indirect costs; vendor agreement terms govern recovery rate; (e) if vendor disputes: escalation per W244 (dispute resolution) and legal review (W230)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 hours per claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1151_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1151_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1151_Task8" name="Recovery Settlement &amp; Post-Recall Financial Close">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Recovery Settlement &amp; Post-Recall Financial Close: (a) vendor remits cost recovery payment (credit note against future invoices, or direct payment); (b) recovery recorded in AP module against recall cost tracker; (c) net recall cost calculated: total recall costs minus vendor recovery; (d) unrecovered costs allocated: if vendor contract covers full recovery → no P&amp;L impact; if partial recovery → net cost allocated to category margin as one-time charge; (e) recall financial record closed and archived; (f) lessons learned feed into vendor scorecard (W44) recall performance metric and vendor contract renewal negotiations (W704)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 hours per recall</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1151_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1151_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1151_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1151_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1151_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1151_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1151_Annotation10" targetRef="W1151_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1151_Flow12" sourceRef="W1151_Start4" targetRef="W1151_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1151_Flow13" sourceRef="W1151_Task5" targetRef="W1151_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1151_Flow14" sourceRef="W1151_Task6" targetRef="W1151_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1151_Flow15" sourceRef="W1151_Task7" targetRef="W1151_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1151_Flow16" sourceRef="W1151_Task8" targetRef="W1151_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1151_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1151_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1151">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_End9_di" bpmnElement="W1151_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1260" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1151_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1151_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1151_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1151_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1151_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1151_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1260" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1151_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W1151_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1224" name="W1224. Vendor Quarterly Business Review, Scorecard Meeting &amp; Strategic Relationship Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly review calendar; or triggered by vendor relationship milestone (new vendor onboarding first review, vendor escalation from W44, contract renewal approaching)
Frequency: Quarterly for top 50 vendors (representing ~70% of COGS); semi-annual for next 50 vendors; annual for remaining ~900 vendors
Volume: ~50 quarterly reviews + ~25 semi-annual reviews + ~900 annual reviews
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Buyer, Supply Planning Analyst, Quality Assurance, Finance Analyst, Vendor Account Manager, VP Merchandising (for top 10 vendors)
Source: workflow W1224 — Vendor Quarterly Business Review, Scorecard Meeting &amp; Strategic Relationship Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1224_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1224_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1224_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1224_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1224_Lane4" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1224_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1224_Start6" name="Quarterly review calendar; or triggered by vendor relationship milestone (new vendor…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1224_Task7" name="Scorecard preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Scorecard preparation (2 weeks before QBR): System compiles vendor scorecard for the trailing quarter: (a) OTIF performance: on-time delivery rate (target ≥ 95%), in-full delivery rate, lead time adherence; (b) Quality: defect rate, return rate, customer complaint rate, product recall incidents; (c) Commercial: total spend vs. prior quarter and prior year, pricing competitiveness vs. market, promotional markdown claims per W161, payment term compliance; (d) Responsiveness: PO acknowledgment time, issue resolution time, query response time; (e) Innovation: new product introductions, category growth contribution, exclusive product development; (f) Compliance: BIR accreditation, product certification (PS mark, ICC), insurance currency, ESG compliance per W195
Responsible (R): System / Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1224_Task8" name="QBR agenda">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager reviews scorecard and prepares QBR agenda: (a) performance highlights and lowlights, (b) open issues from prior QBR — status of agreed actions, (c) upcoming seasonal demand forecast and required capacity, (d) new product opportunities or SKU rationalization discussion, (e) promotional calendar alignment for next quarter, (f) pricing review: any cost increase requests, competitive pricing concerns, (g) relationship health: any disputes, payment issues, or communication gaps
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1224_Task9" name="QBR meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: QBR meeting (in-person for top 20 vendors; virtual for others): (a) Category Manager presents BuildRight scorecard; Vendor Account Manager presents their perspective: production capacity, new products, market trends, cost drivers; (b) discuss open action items from prior QBR — verify closure or escalate; (c) align on next quarter&#x27;s demand forecast and promotional calendar; (d) negotiate any pricing changes — Category Manager has authority for ≤ 3% price increase acceptance; larger increases require VP Merchandising approval; (e) agree on new actions and owners with deadlines
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Vendor Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising (top 10)
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1224_Task10" name="Strategic vendor planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Strategic vendor planning (top 10 vendors only, annual): VP Merchandising and Category Manager conduct strategic planning session with vendor&#x27;s senior leadership: (a) 3-year category growth plan, (b) exclusive product development roadmap, (c) joint business plan with shared KPIs, (d) technology integration roadmap (EDI, vendor portal enhancements per VS-03.4), (e) sustainability commitments per W195
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CEO (for #1 vendor)
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1224_Task11" name="Post-QBR documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-QBR documentation: Category Manager documents QBR minutes: (a) scorecard results, (b) agreed actions with owners and deadlines, (c) pricing agreements, (d) demand forecast shared with vendor, (e) any escalations or disputes; distributes to internal stakeholders (Buyer, Supply Planning, Finance, QA) and vendor within 48 hours
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1224_Task12" name="Action item tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Action item tracking: Buyer and Supply Planning Analyst track QBR action items to closure: (a) weekly check on overdue items, (b) escalate non-responsive vendor actions to Category Manager, (c) system sends automated reminders to action owners 3 days before deadline
Responsible (R): Buyer / Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1224_Task13" name="Semi-annual vendor tier classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Semi-annual vendor tier classification: Category Manager reviews vendor tier classification: (a) Strategic (top 50): QBR + joint business planning + preferred terms, (b) Preferred (next 100): semi-annual review + competitive terms, (c) Transactional (remaining ~850): annual review + standard terms; vendors may be promoted or demoted based on scorecard trajectory
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1224_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1224_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1224_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1224_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1224_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1224_Annotation15" targetRef="W1224_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1224_Flow17" sourceRef="W1224_Start6" targetRef="W1224_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1224_Flow18" sourceRef="W1224_Task7" targetRef="W1224_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1224_Flow19" sourceRef="W1224_Task8" targetRef="W1224_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1224_Flow20" sourceRef="W1224_Task9" targetRef="W1224_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1224_Flow21" sourceRef="W1224_Task10" targetRef="W1224_Task11" />
