    <bpmn:process id="W_W1303" name="W1303. Vendor Rebate, Co-Op Advertising Fund &amp; Promotional Incentive Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly rebate calculation cycle; or co-op advertising campaign execution; or promotional incentive claim from vendor
Frequency: Quarterly rebate settlements; monthly co-op advertising reconciliation; promotional incentives per sale event
Volume: ~200 vendors with rebate agreements; ~50 vendors with co-op advertising arrangements; ~PHP 800M–1.2B in annual vendor rebates and co-op income
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Finance Analyst, Marketing Manager, Buyer, Vendor Account Manager, AP Clerk
Source: workflow W1303 — Vendor Rebate, Co-Op Advertising Fund &amp; Promotional Incentive Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1303_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1303_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1303_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1303_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1303_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1303_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1303_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1303_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1303_Lane3" name="Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1303_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1303_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1303_Start5" name="Quarterly rebate calculation cycle; or co-op advertising campaign execution; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1303_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1303_Task6" name="Rebate agreement setup &amp; tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Rebate agreement setup &amp; tracking: (a) during annual vendor negotiations (W44), Category Manager negotiates rebate terms: (i) volume rebate tiers (e.g., PHP 0–50M = 1%, PHP 50–100M = 2%, &gt; PHP 100M = 3%), (ii) co-op advertising fund percentage (e.g., 3% of annual purchases), (iii) promotional incentive schedule (e.g., PHP 200K per bi-monthly catalog placement); (b) Finance Analyst enters rebate agreement parameters into Oracle Trade Management (fit-gap B10): tier thresholds, percentage rates, settlement frequency, eligible product categories, exclusions; (c) system tracks cumulative purchases per vendor against rebate tiers in real-time; (d) system alerts Category Manager when vendor approaches next rebate tier threshold
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 hours/vendor during annual negotiation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1303_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1303_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1303_Task7" name="Quarterly rebate calculation &amp; claim">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly rebate calculation &amp; claim: (a) at quarter-end, system calculates earned rebate per vendor: (i) cumulative purchases for the quarter × applicable rebate rate, (ii) if annual rebate: system calculates projected annual rebate based on YTD purchases × annualized rate; (b) Finance Analyst reviews calculated rebates: (i) verify purchase volume against AP records per W7, (ii) verify eligible products (some agreements exclude consignment, clearance, or imported items), (iii) verify no double-counting across entities (BuildRight Depot purchases vs. Logistics purchases); (c) system generates rebate claim report per vendor with supporting purchase detail; (d) Category Manager reviews and approves claim; (e) claim transmitted to vendor via supplier portal; (f) vendor reviews and confirms or disputes; (g) upon vendor confirmation: system generates AP credit memo or vendor payment per agreement (credit against future invoices or direct payment)
Responsible (R): System / Finance Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1303_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1303_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1303_Task8" name="Co-op advertising fund reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Co-op advertising fund reconciliation: Monthly, Marketing Manager and Category Manager reconcile co-op advertising fund: (a) system calculates co-op fund earned: monthly purchases from vendor × co-op fund %; (b) system tracks co-op advertising expenditures by vendor: (i) catalog placement costs (per page, per edition), (ii) social media advertising spend featuring vendor&#x27;s products, (iii) in-store display costs (signage, fixtures, point-of-purchase materials), (iv) digital advertising costs (website banners, search ads); (c) reconcile earned fund vs. spent amount: (i) if earned &gt; spent: BuildRight has surplus co-op fund to spend on vendor&#x27;s advertising, (ii) if spent &gt; earned: BuildRight may owe vendor reimbursement or excess counts against future fund; (d) Marketing Manager plans next month&#x27;s co-op advertising allocation per vendor based on fund balance and promotional calendar
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1303_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1303_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1303_Task9" name="Promotional incentive claim processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Promotional incentive claim processing: Per promotional event: (a) before sale event: Category Manager negotiates promotional incentives with vendor: markdown money (vendor subsidizes discount on their products), display allowance (payment for featured placement), bonus stock (vendor provides free product for every X units purchased); (b) promotional incentive terms entered in ERP with promotional event ID; (c) during promotion: system tracks promotional sales by vendor — items sold at promotional price, discount amount, display placement verification; (d) post-promotion: system calculates total promotional incentive earned per vendor: (i) markdown money: total units sold at discount × vendor subsidy per unit, (ii) display allowance: per-placement fee × number of stores displaying, (iii) bonus stock: units earned × cost per unit; (e) Category Manager submits promotional incentive claim to vendor with supporting sales data; (f) vendor confirms and issues credit or payment
Responsible (R): Category Manager / System
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 hours per promotional event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1303_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1303_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1303_Task10" name="Annual vendor program ROI analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual vendor program ROI analysis: Annual, Category Manager and Finance Analyst evaluate vendor program ROI: (a) total rebates, co-op income, and promotional incentives earned per vendor, (b) as % of purchases from that vendor (benchmark: 2–5% of purchases), (c) vendor compliance rate (claims disputed, payments delayed), (d) comparison: vendors with rebate programs vs. vendors without (are rebate vendors giving BuildRight better net pricing or just inflating gross price to fund rebates?); (e) recommend to VP Merchandising: negotiate higher rebate rates with top vendors, replace underperforming rebate programs with flat net pricing, or expand co-op advertising programs
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1303_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1303_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1303_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1303_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1303_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-248 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Performance &amp; Contracts (PA-03.3).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
